Subject: [PATCH] Follow MaterialYou's color scheme for automatic popup styling

GNOME Shell's built-in style variant remains dark with a custom User Themes
stylesheet. MaterialYou independently generates light CSS from the desktop
preference, so using the built-in variant produces dark surfaces with dark
text. Follow MaterialYou's input when its stylesheet is active; retain the
upstream selection for other themes and explicit popup style overrides.

--- a/components/popup/index.js
+++ b/components/popup/index.js
@@ -504,6 +504,10 @@
         if (lower_uri.includes('yaru'))
             return lower_uri.includes('dark') ? 2 : 1;
 
+        if (lower_uri.includes('/materialyou/gnome-shell/'))
+            return this.interface_settings.get_string('color-scheme') ===
+                'prefer-dark' ? 2 : 1;
+
         const shell_style = Main.getStyleVariant();
         if (shell_style === 'light')
             return 1;
